<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Cash wheat bids drop.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Cash wheat bids drop.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash spring wheat bids were lower again Tuesday, which kept farmer selling light, spring wheat dealers said.</p>
<p>Planting continued to advance throughout the northern spring wheat areas and may begin soon in areas bordering the Red River in North Dakota and Minnesota.</p>
<p>&quot;We are hoping by the end of the week to get started,&quot; a North Dakota dealer said.</p>
<p>In Montana, planting advanced rapidly but hot weather was needed to encourage growth.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat settled four to 10 cents lower with July off six cents at $4.20 a bushel.</p>
